// uax29_tests.nv — the annex's own answers, run whole.
//
// `GraphemeBreakTest.txt` and `WordBreakTest.txt` are what UAX #29
// means by conformant: every case is a run of codepoints with `÷`
// where a boundary falls and `×` where one does not, and an
// implementation that agrees with every line of them agrees with the
// annex rather than with somebody's reading of it.
//
// WHAT RUNS HERE AND WHAT RUNS IN VERIFICATION.  The sample below is
// committed — the opening cases of each file, which are the rules in
// their simplest form, then a fixed stride through the rest — so
// `novo test` proves conformance with no download and no network.  The
// WHOLE files run through the same reader when `NOVO_UCD` names a
// directory holding them:
//
//     NOVO_UCD=/path/to/ucd novo test tests/uax29_tests.nv
//
// Shipping the reader rather than a list of expected answers is what
// makes the second command possible at all, and it is why the sample is
// generated by `tools/gen_conformance.py` rather than typed.

use std.env
use std.fs
use std.list
use std.str
use std.test
use ugrapheme

// U+00F7 DIVISION SIGN, which the annex writes where a boundary falls.
const DIVIDE = 0x00F7

// U+00D7 MULTIPLICATION SIGN, where one does not.
const TIMES = 0x00D7

